[agent] ## Missing interface capability — online/low-latency serving
[agent] I could **not** fulfill the "make features available for online/real-time lookup" requirement through the allowed interface, and per the task rules I'm reporting it rather than working around it.
[agent] - On GCP, offline vs. online is distinguished by **Vertex AI Feature Store**: a *Feature Group* over the BigQuery table (offline) plus a *Feature Online Store* + *Feature View* (online low-latency serving).
[agent] - Those resources are exposed in gcloud **only under `gcloud beta ai …` / `gcloud alpha ai …`** (`feature-online-stores`, `feature-groups`, `feature-views`). The GA `gcloud ai` surface available here has **no** feature-store subgroups (only custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index/-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs).
[agent] - The Bash allowlist blocks `gcloud beta`/`gcloud alpha` as off-interface, and no other allowed tool (`bq`, `gcloud storage/monitoring`) can create an online store.
[agent] So the offline feature table exists and is readable in BigQuery (the platform's offline read path), but the online store cannot be created with the GA `gcloud ai` CLI as configured. I set an `online_enabled=true` label on the table as a best-effort marker, but there is no actual online-serving resource — that capability is genuinely absent from the permitted interface.
